WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:04.540
Cobra Kai's third season is full of tension
and surprises.

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:09.470
Kreese takes over Cobra Kai with "no mercy,"
Daniel and Johnny team up, and all three sensei

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:13.860
confront their pasts as they prepare to settle
their present-day differences.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:18.180
Let's break down the explosive ending, and
what it may mean for season four.

00:00:19.289 --> 00:00:24.199
After Robby makes Miyagi-Do infamous for what
happened during the school melee in season

00:00:24.199 --> 00:00:30.269
2, Daniel finds that his karate-themed advertisements
aren't so cute anymore, as his car sales begin

00:00:30.269 --> 00:00:31.269
to drag.

00:00:31.269 --> 00:00:36.980
His top competitor, Tom Cole, secures an exclusive
distribution deal with Doyona and offers to

00:00:36.980 --> 00:00:40.000
buy Daniel's dealership at a bargain price.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.440
But Daniel decides to take a trip to Japan
instead.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:48.640
After an inauspicious meeting with Doyona,
Daniel visits Mr. Miyagi's home in Okinawa

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:53.690
and reunites with Kumiko, the young woman
he defended and had a romantic relationship

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:55.850
with in The Karate Kid Part II.

00:00:55.850 --> 00:01:01.460
Kumiko has several surprises in store for
Daniel at Tomi village, including Mr. Miyagi's

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:06.600
old love letters to her late aunt Yukie and
a visit from the now-grown woman he rescued

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.579
from a typhoon as a child.

00:01:08.579 --> 00:01:13.890
She's now VP of international sales at Doyona,
and as a long overdue reward for saving her

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:19.350
life so many years before, she steps in to
save his business relationship with the company.

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:24.149
Not only does the LaRusso Auto Group come
out of their PR nightmare relatively unscathed

00:01:24.149 --> 00:01:29.009
in the end, but they also convince Anoush
to return to their team, and find that cousin

00:01:29.009 --> 00:01:31.960
Louie is actually a pretty solid salesman.

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:37.060
With the dealership on solid ground once again,
Daniel will be able to focus on his more personal

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:38.790
matters going forward.

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:44.219
Another familiar face Kumiko brings back into
the picture is that of Chozen, who Daniel

00:01:44.219 --> 00:01:47.540
defeated in a brutal fight in The Karate Kid
Part II.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:51.579
Rather than holding a grudge, however, Chozen
wants to make amends.

00:01:51.579 --> 00:01:56.869
Chozen reveals that his sensei Sato was also
trained by Miyagi's teacher, so he has inherited

00:01:56.869 --> 00:02:02.399
several artifacts from Miyagi's dojo and wants
to test whether Miyagi really taught Daniel

00:02:02.399 --> 00:02:03.840
everything he knew.

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:09.170
During a match, Chozen stuns Daniel by striking
several pressure points and disabling his

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:12.560
limbs, a maneuver he attributes to Miyagi's
teachings.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:17.209
After pinning Daniel, Chozen ends the fight
by honking his nose, which is a playful nod

00:02:17.209 --> 00:02:21.260
to how Daniel ended their vicious bout so
many years before.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:25.950
Chozen admits he has felt shame for his behavior
back then and is relieved to learn that Daniel

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:27.120
has forgiven him.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:32.170
In return, Chozen agrees to train Daniel in
Miyagi's powerful move and also gives him

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:35.510
a cherished scroll from Miyagi's collection
to take home.

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:40.290
Not only does Daniel walk away with a newfound
peace agreement with Chozen, he's also armed

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:43.790
with a very effective new defense technique.

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:47.200
"If only every rivalry could end like this."

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:52.379
In addition to saving his business and learning
a new trick in Japan, Daniel also gets some

00:02:52.379 --> 00:02:53.930
closure with Kumiko.

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:58.519
Though the two had an intense connection in
Okinawa all those decades ago, they lost touch

00:02:58.519 --> 00:03:01.160
with one another and moved on with their lives.

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:05.110
The two lament the fact that they might have
kept in contact more easily in the modern

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:08.030
era of social media, but they part on great
terms.

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:12.590
Kumiko isn't the only ex that Daniel gets
to finally say goodbye to, either.

00:03:12.590 --> 00:03:16.799
Ali also returns to the picture after she
and Johnny reconnect on Facebook.

00:03:16.799 --> 00:03:21.100
Though Johnny has finally begun a romantic
relationship with Miguel's mom Carmen, he

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:24.159
can't resist the chance to catch up with his
high school flame.

00:03:24.159 --> 00:03:28.349
The two spend a whole day together having
fun at lunch and an arcade, and she takes

00:03:28.349 --> 00:03:31.980
him to a country club party that Daniel also
attends.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:35.069
“You remember Johnny Lawrence, right?"

00:03:35.069 --> 00:03:37.790
"How can I forget?"

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:43.120
Ali is bemused to find her former flames fighting
just like old times but correctly calls them

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:46.049
out for being more alike than they'd like
to admit.

00:03:46.049 --> 00:03:50.860
She also accepts Daniel's apology for ending
things so abruptly and thanks Johnny for making

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:53.819
her feel young again before wishing him well
with Carmen.

00:03:53.819 --> 00:03:58.170
The memory of fighting over Ali has always
been a point of contention for Daniel and

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:01.680
Johnny, but now that the two have gotten a
chance to talk things out with her, they can

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:03.969
finally let go of that piece of their animosity.

00:04:03.969 --> 00:04:09.749
"And the truth is, you guys are more alike
than you want to admit."

00:04:10.749 --> 00:04:14.469
Johnny and Carmen aren't the only new lovebirds
taking flight this season.

00:04:14.469 --> 00:04:20.329
It looks like Miguel and Sam are also ready
to octopi some space together again, too.

00:04:20.329 --> 00:04:24.790
After training with Johnny, Miguel is back
in fighting shape and returns to school.

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:29.500
Sam apologizes to Miguel, helps raise money
for his treatments, and even shows him around

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:30.560
Miyagi-Do.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:35.070
The sight of them together might make Robby
incensed, and it even raises eyebrows with

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:38.449
Daniel, but Sam and Miguel share more than
just some smooches.

00:04:38.449 --> 00:04:42.470
Together, they hatch a plan to unite their
dojos for the greater good.

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:46.680
Meanwhile, Demetri and Yasmin have become
unlikely kissing buddies -- not that she'd

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:51.360
ever admit that in public, of course -- and
something is definitely brewing between Robby

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:52.440
and Tory.

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:57.090
After Robby is released from juvenile detention,
he and Tory bond over their equally crummy

00:04:57.090 --> 00:05:02.300
upbringings and their mutual dissatisfaction
with the idea of Miguel and Sam getting back

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:03.300
together.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:07.120
Whether these two will combine their anger
to form a butt-kicking power couple remains

00:05:07.120 --> 00:05:11.460
to be seen, but based on the looks they give
each other in the final episodes, we wouldn't

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:15.620
be surprised if their relationship is about
to heat up off the mat.

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:21.400
At first, Miguel has trouble convincing the
members of Johnny's new Eagle Fang dojo to

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:24.530
join forces with Sam's Miyagi-Do members.

00:05:24.530 --> 00:05:28.300
But once the Cobra Kais attack them all at
their Christmas party, the battle lines are

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:29.669
officially drawn.

00:05:29.669 --> 00:05:35.250
This means former besties-turned-rivals Mitch
and Chris and Bert and Nathaniel can finally

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:38.830
fight together again, instead of forcing themselves
to hate each other.

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:42.590
Perhaps the most surprising member to join
this new team is Hawk.

00:05:42.590 --> 00:05:47.130
He is initially poised to be Cobra Kai's new
champion and takes Kreese's tough teachings

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:51.820
to heart, even breaking Demetri's arm during
an off-the-mat confrontation.

00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:56.380
All season long, though, Hawk watches with
disdain as Kreese recruits most of his least

00:05:56.380 --> 00:06:01.810
favorite people to join the dojo, including
his former bully Kyler and Robby, who Hawk

00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:04.340
still blames for what happened to Miguel.

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:07.090
"Look, I know some of these guys, and they're,"

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:11.500
"Natural athletes, which is exactly what's
been missing in our dojo."

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:16.400
Hawk participates in the siege on Miyagi-Do,
but upon seeing his teammates attacking his

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:21.340
former friends, he decides to switch sides
and defends Demetri against having his arm

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:22.490
broken again.

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:27.510
He takes Demetri's side at Miyagi-Do for the
first day of dual training with Eagle Fang,

00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:32.319
making it clear that these two are finally
ready to fight side by side after so much

00:06:32.319 --> 00:06:33.319
turmoil.

00:06:34.319 --> 00:06:38.910
After the Cobra Kais attack the unsuspecting
kids at Miyagi-Do, Johnny decides to confront

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:41.590
his former sensei once and for all.

00:06:41.590 --> 00:06:46.440
He's surprised to find his son Robby at the
dojo rising to Kreese's defense, but Johnny

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:50.550
still engages Kreese in a fight that very
nearly turns deadly.

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:55.840
Robby discourages Johnny from using a sai
on Kreese after he gains the upper hand, and

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:58.569
Kreese makes him pay for that moment of mercy.

00:06:58.569 --> 00:07:03.199
After Robby himself tries to pick a fight
with Johnny, Johnny accidentally knocks him

00:07:03.199 --> 00:07:07.699
out against a locker, and Kreese nearly chokes
Johnny to death.

00:07:07.699 --> 00:07:12.580
However, Daniel arrives in the nick of time
and kicks Kreese off of Johnny.

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:17.840
After a brief fight, Daniel uses Miyagi's
disabling move to stop Kreese in his tracks.

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:21.880
Kreese suggests that instead of this turning
into a deathmatch, they finish the fight by

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:26.340
entering their students in the All Valley
Tournament they all stood up to save.

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:30.870
If Cobra Kai loses, Kreese promises to disappear
from town for good.

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:35.819
While Johnny and Daniel unite to take Kreese
down, however, Kreese maintains one last trick

00:07:35.819 --> 00:07:36.819
up his sleeve.

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:43.259
Throughout Cobra Kai season three, we finally
learn why Kreese is so hellbent on his "strike

00:07:43.259 --> 00:07:45.680
first" and "no mercy" philosophies.

00:07:45.680 --> 00:07:50.060
After enduring the death of his mother and
bullying in his workplace, young Kreese finally

00:07:50.060 --> 00:07:54.990
fought back when one of his tormentors hit
his girlfriend, Betsy, who then became Kreese's

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:55.990
girlfriend.

00:07:55.990 --> 00:08:00.750
He signed up for a tour in Vietnam shortly
after, and was recruited for a covert mission

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:03.669
alongside his friends Ponytail and Twig.

00:08:03.669 --> 00:08:07.189
Tragically, the entire unit was captured on
that mission.

00:08:07.189 --> 00:08:11.639
Ponytail was immediately executed, while the
others were made to fight one another to the

00:08:11.639 --> 00:08:13.699
death above a pit of snakes.

00:08:13.699 --> 00:08:19.240
Kreese's captain, who regularly accused him
of cowardice, was chosen to fight Twig, and

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:21.820
Kreese volunteered to take Twig's place.

00:08:21.820 --> 00:08:26.590
The captain nearly defeated Kreese after he
revealed Beth had died in a car accident,

00:08:26.590 --> 00:08:28.690
but Kreese gained the upper hand.

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:33.400
Even as they were saved by air support, Kreese
kicked the captain into the pit and declared

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:36.380
he'd finally learned his lesson: Show no mercy.

00:08:36.380 --> 00:08:41.010
Twig, who may not have seen Kreese kick the
captain, told Kreese that he owed him a life

00:08:41.010 --> 00:08:43.979
debt and would always be there for whatever
Kreese needed.

00:08:43.979 --> 00:08:47.490
Now, it appears Kreese is finally ready to
collect.

00:08:47.490 --> 00:08:51.709
After Kreese makes his deal with Johnny and
Daniel to settle their disputes at the tournament,

00:08:51.709 --> 00:08:57.300
he makes a call to an old friend while holding
a photo of himself with Ponytail and Twig.

